// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`immutable binary inspection > explains how to replace a source snapshot with an imported file before collection > binary input guide 1`] = `"Select an imported single file with assetId, not a source directory or parameters.path. Directory imports expose binary child assets through security_scope. For an older source snapshot, the coordinator can use security_command action import-member with source assetId, exact manifest path and label; no Host re-import is needed. Delegated analysts ask the coordinator to select or register the file. identity requires parameters "{}". hex and strings accept byte offset and length; length defaults to maxOutputBytes/8 and cannot exceed it. strings also accepts minLength (default 4), encoding ascii or utf16le (default ascii); only printable ASCII characters are extracted. Overlap pages to check strings crossing a page edge. Input is the immutable imported artifact; no executable is needed."`;
